      "message": "Is this really cleaner than just duplicating the definitions of `PERSISTENT_RAM_SIG` and `struct persistent_ram_buffer` in the hypervisor code with a \"Copied from ...\" comment?\n\nBoth definitions are very simple, so duplicating them seems much less fragile than compiling the entire `ram_core.c` into this binary (and of course much simpler as well)?\n\nAlso that would be closer to a really clean future solution (which we are avoiding for now, as we are avoiding changes in generic parts of kernel), i.e.: simply moving those definitions from `ram_core.c` to a header under `include/linux/`? (I mean, in both that case and with duplicated definitions, the hypervisor code would directly use those definitions instead of these PKVM_RAMOOPS_xxx macros.)",
